# Vendor binaries. Endgame Gear's proprietary Windows software, kept local and
# never published. SHA-256 of every build analysed is pinned in notes/binaries.md.
*.exe
old-config-executables/
old-firmware-executables/
files/

# Ghidra projects and extraction output
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock
ghidra_projects/
*.jsonl

# Extracted firmware images
*.bin
*.hex

# Build output
build/
build-san/
.build/
cmake-build-*/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.a
*.dSYM/
.cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code local overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# Analysis working directory: Ghidra logs, resource dumps of vendor firmware,
# exported decompilation. Scripts live in Tools/; this holds only their output.
.analysis/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Mutation-run transcripts. Reproducible by `ctest -R mutants`; the RESULT
# belongs in a commit message, the 76-line transcript does not.
mutants-run.log
mut*.log

# Fixtures Tests/test_auditclaims.py plants in the real notes/ tree to measure
# the citation checker. Deleted in a `finally`, which a kill does not run --
# so they are ignored here too, and Tools/no-mutants.sh refuses a commit while
# one is present. A planted DEFECT reaching a commit is the failure mode.
notes/zzz-planted-*.md

# The bootloader entry receipt (Sources/EGGFlashCore/include/egg/Provenance.h).
# `enter-bootloader` writes it to $HOME, not to the working directory -- a
# Finder-launched .app runs with a cwd of "/", so a cwd-relative receipt could
# never be written from the GUI and every flash from the app would refuse. It
# is listed here anyway for the HOME-less fallback path, and because a
# committed receipt would vouch for an A1 3A entry that happened on someone
# else's machine.
.egg-mouse-entry-receipt

# Backup provenance sidecars. The images themselves are already ignored above
# (*.bin); these say where one came from and are equally local.
*.bin.origin

# ============================================================================
# Untracked 2026-09-07. Everything below was PREVIOUSLY COMMITTED and has been
# removed from the index with `git rm --cached`; the files are still on disk.
# ============================================================================

# Working files. Process, not product.
#
# CLAUDE.md is a local rules file and working-memory.md is the working state of
# whoever is doing the work (§1.7). Neither is documentation for a user of this
# software. The protocol findings they point at live in notes/, which stays
# public, and the rules themselves are published as engineering-rules.md at the
# repo root, which CLAUDE.md is a symlink to.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated because it is a real cost: git is no longer the backup
# for working-memory.md. §1.7 exists because a session that dies takes its
# head with it -- that argument is unchanged, and the file is now one `rm`
# from gone. See §1.7, which was amended to match.
CLAUDE.md
working-memory.md
.claude/

# Quarantined evidence (§1.1a). The root log.txt was found to misdescribe what
# was actually done at the device, so it is unreliable in full rather than in
# part. Kept on disk because it holds in-progress corrections; never published,
# because a file that misdescribes what was done is worse than no file at all.
# The leading slash keeps this entry about the root file specifically;
# windows-run/log.txt is a different file and is untracked separately below.
/log.txt

# CTest scratch output. Regenerated by every run; was committed by accident.
/Testing/

# Machine baselines from `Tools/verify-environment.sh --save`. Each describes
# ONE machine at ONE moment -- OS build, compiler build, attached interfaces.
# Regenerate your own rather than read someone else's.
baseline-*.txt

# Loose working images and scratch. Device backups live here; they are
# irreplaceable, so this ignores them rather than anything deleting them.
/local/

# ============================================================================
# Untracked 2026-09-08. Previously committed; removed from the index with
# `git rm --cached`, and still on disk.
# ============================================================================

# Session material from the Windows run. The .pcapng captures stay tracked --
# they are the bytes, and every [O] claim in notes/ rests on them. These three
# are the human record of the same session and are not needed to check any of
# it: log.txt is single-sourced and only its section 05 was ever filled in
# (§1.1a), the screenshots are photographs of one machine's screen, and
# CAPTURE-STEPS.md is the operator's script for a run that has already happened.
#
# CONSEQUENCE. notes/ and the source comments still cite the screenshots by
# name as the source of a setting's range or label. Those citations now point
# outside the published tree: the claim they support stays checkable against
# the captures, but the screenshot itself is no longer there to look at.
windows-run/log.txt
windows-run/screenshots/
docs/CAPTURE-STEPS.md
